    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: move date-derived owner values to a fiscal-year basis (FY starts 1 July)\n\n**New `FiscalYear` utility** (`util/FiscalYear.java`) \u2014 owns the single responsibility of the fiscal-year calendar:\n- `of(date)` \u2014 the four-digit fiscal year, numbered by the calendar year it *ends* in (1 Jul 2026 \u2013 30 Jun 2027 \u2192 2027).\n- `yearSegment(date)` \u2014 the two-digit segment (`27`) reused by identifiers.\n- `label(date)` \u2014 the `FY<YY>` string (`\"FY27\"`), null-safe.\n- `elapsedYears(start, end)` \u2014 whole fiscal years elapsed (count of 1 July boundaries crossed).\n\n**`Owner` model** now delegates all fiscal-year logic to that utility rather than duplicating date math:\n- Added `getFiscalYear()` \u2192 `FiscalYear.label(registrationDate)`, exposed as the new `fiscalYear` response field.\n- `getMembershipNumber()` \u2014 its `M<YY>` segment now uses `FiscalYear.yearSegment(...)` instead of `registrationDate.getYear() % 100`, so the identifier's year segment is the fiscal year.\n- Replaced `getTenureDays()` (365-day window via `ChronoUnit.DAYS`) with `getTenureFiscalYears()` (elapsed fiscal years). The tenure membership-points rule now awards its 3 points at \u2265 1 elapsed fiscal year. The unused `ChronoUnit` import was dropped.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `fiscalYear` property to the `Owner` schema and updated the `membershipNumber` / `membershipPoints` descriptions to reflect the fiscal-year basis. The DTO is generated from this spec at build time, and MapStruct auto-maps `getFiscalYear()` by name, so no mapper change was needed.\n\nVerification: `mvnw test` \u2192 BUILD SUCCESS, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. The audit log confirms behaviour \u2014 a 2026-09-21 registration (FY2027) now yields `membershipNumber=NSW-...-M27`, and `fiscalYear` matches the test's `FY\\d{2}` assertion.\n\nOne convention decision worth flagging: I numbered each fiscal year by the calendar year it **ends** in (the standard Australian government convention), which the acceptance test's `FY\\d{2}` regex doesn't pin down. If you intended the *start*-year convention (Jul 2026 \u2192 FY26), that's a one-line change in `FiscalYear.of`.",
